# Purpose: documentation for the benchmark simulation data shipped with the package (R CMD check requires datasets to be documented)

#' Benchmark simulation dataset collection shipped with the package
#'
#' @description
#' 30 datasets pre-generated by the \code{scenario} route of the three demo facades
#' (\code{\link{mlr3HTE_demo_continuous}}, \code{\link{mlr3HTE_demo_binary}},
#' \code{\link{mlr3HTE_demo_surv}}) across \strong{10 designs x 3 outcome types},
#' each with \code{n = 2000} and a fixed seed, packaged in
#' \code{data/mlr3hte_bench_data.rda} and shipped with the package.
#'
#' The reason for fixing on one dataset: methodology comparisons are only comparable
#' on the same dataset. If each analysis re-simulates on its own, random sampling
#' noise gets mixed into the difference between two learners and the conclusion cannot
#' be replicated.
#'
#' The four structural dimensions are mutually independent, so you can fix the others
#' and change only one for comparison:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{Study design}{\code{rct} (randomized, no confounding) and \code{obs}
#'     (observational, with confounding)}
#'   \item{Confounding form}{\code{none} / \code{linear} / \code{nonlinear}}
#'   \item{Effect-heterogeneity form}{\code{linear} (CATE is a linear function of
#'     covariates) and \code{nonlinear} (contains \code{sin} and a quadratic term)}
#'   \item{Whether a variable is shared}{\code{shared = TRUE} means a covariate exists
#'     that enters both the treatment-assignment model and the true CATE, i.e. a
#'     confounder that is also an effect modifier}
#' }
#'
#' @docType data
#' @name mlr3hte_bench_data
#' @format A named list of length 30. The names are \code{<scenario id>.<outcome>}, e.g.
#'   \code{"obs_nonlin_nonlin_sharedT.survival"}; each element has the same structure
#'   as the return value of the \code{scenario} route of
#'   \code{\link{mlr3HTE_demo_continuous}}:
#'   \describe{
#'     \item{\code{X}}{A data.frame of covariates (\code{age} / \code{lac} / \code{tumor} / \code{sex})}
#'     \item{\code{A}}{Treatment indicator (0/1)}
#'     \item{\code{Y}}{Outcome; a \code{survival::Surv} object for survival outcomes}
#'     \item{\code{tau}}{Per-individual true CATE}
#'     \item{\code{ate}}{True ATE, equal to \code{mean(tau)}}
#'     \item{\code{ps_true}}{True propensity score; always 0.5 for RCT scenarios}
#'     \item{\code{tau_rmst} / \code{ate_rmst}}{RMST-scale truth for survival outcomes;
#'       \code{NULL} for other outcomes}
#'     \item{\code{meta}}{Structural labels and generation parameters}
#'   }
#' @usage data(mlr3hte_bench_data)
#' @source Generated by the demo facades' \code{scenario} route; the generation script
#'   is \code{data-raw/bench.R} in the repository (that directory is listed in
#'   \code{.Rbuildignore} and not installed with the package).
#' @seealso \code{\link{mlr3HTE_demo_continuous}},
#'   \code{\link{mlr3HTE_demo_binary}}, \code{\link{mlr3HTE_demo_surv}}
#'   (\code{source = "bundled"} reads this collection, \code{catalog = TRUE} lists it).
#' @keywords datasets
#' @examples
#' \donttest{
#' names(mlr3hte_bench_data)[1:3]
#' mlr3HTE_demo_continuous(catalog = TRUE, source = "bundled")[1:3, ]
#' }
NULL
